== How to enter flash mode ==
The tablet has no reliable key combination for the Rockchip loader. From Android with USB debugging enabled:
<syntaxhighlight lang="shell-session">
$ adb reboot bootloader
$ rkdeveloptool ld
</syntaxhighlight>
From postmarketOS, <code>sudo systemctl reboot --reboot-argument=loader</code>. The loader is the Rockchip "rockusb" protocol, handled by [[Rkdeveloptool|rkdeveloptool]].

If the tablet only reaches the stock recovery ("No command"), its menu (hold Power, tap Volume Up) has "update rkimage from external storage", which installs an unsigned Rockchip <code>update.img</code> from the microSD card (CRC-checked only).

== Installation ==
postmarketOS is installed on a microSD card; the kernel goes into the eMMC <code>boot</code> partition. The bootloader is never modified. '''Back up the eMMC first''' (<code>rkdeveloptool rl 0 0x50000 emmc-head.bin</code> covers all partitions up to <code>backup</code>).

<syntaxhighlight lang="shell-session">
$ pmbootstrap init                      # archos-oxygen101
$ pmbootstrap install --sdcard=/dev/sdX
$ pmbootstrap export
$ adb reboot bootloader
$ rkdeveloptool wl 0x16000 /tmp/postmarketOS-export/boot.img
$ rkdeveloptool rd
</syntaxhighlight>

To dual boot, write <code>boot.img</code> to the recovery partition instead (<code>0x26000</code>) and boot postmarketOS with <code>adb reboot recovery</code>.

Kernel upgrades are written to the eMMC by a <code>mkinitfs_postprocess</code> hook of the device package, to whichever of <code>boot</code>/<code>recovery</code> already holds a postmarketOS image.

== Bootloader notes ==
The stock loader is Rockchip U-Boot 2014.04 (<code>rkdevelop</code> branch). It boots Android v0 boot images (page size 16384) from the partitions of the Rockchip parameter block (no GPT), and:
* ignores the load addresses in the image header;
* loads the device tree from the "second" section, which must be a Rockchip RSCE resource image holding <code>rk-kernel.dtb</code> (otherwise it falls back to the vendor DTB in the <code>resource</code> partition);
* takes the kernel command line from the parameter block, so the kernel uses <code>CONFIG_CMDLINE_EXTEND</code>;
* does not verify signatures;
* falls back to <code>recovery</code> when <code>boot</code> cannot be loaded.

The mainline RK3288 reboot modes match it: <code>recovery</code>, <code>bootloader</code> (fastboot) and <code>loader</code> (rockusb), as in <code>systemctl reboot --reboot-argument=recovery</code>. They need a kernel patch: the RC5T619 restart handler power-cycles the SoC, which clears the reboot-mode register, so it is skipped for reboots into a mode.

